from review_helpers import *
review('SCENARIO-OCBO-001',[
('The Building Permit checklist lists a notarized application letter; notarized Unified Building Permit Form with Civil/Architectural plans signed/sealed by a licensed Civil Engineer/Architect (5 accomplished form copies); Architectural, Civil/Structural, and Sanitary/Plumbing forms (3 form copies and 5 plan sets each). Civil/Structural plans identify a licensed Civil Engineer; Sanitary/Plumbing identifies a licensed Sanitary Engineer/Master Plumber. Architectural plans must be signed/sealed by the hired licensed professional.',[(2,'CHECKLIST','5 sets of Plans')]),
('Electrical: 3 accomplished form copies and 5 plan sets, signed/sealed by a Licensed Professional Electrical Engineer. Electronics: 2 form copies and 5 plan sets, signed/sealed by a Licensed Electronics Engineer. Mechanical row is internally inconsistent: it says 6-7 sets Mechanical Plans, then 2 form copies and 5 plan sets, and names Licensed Electronics Engineer. These mechanical quantities/professional designation require official clarification rather than replacement with an assumed rule.',[(3,'6. Electrical','9. Zoning')]),
('The checklist also lists Zoning Location Clearance and BFP Fire Safety Evaluation Certificate (1 original and 1 photocopy each); certified true copies of land title, property tax declaration and current real-property-tax receipt (1 original and 1 photocopy each); owner/applicant ID with 3 specimen signatures (1 photocopy); PRC IDs, current PTR and TIN of signing professionals (1 photocopy per professional).',[(3,'9. Zoning','per signing professional')]),
('Other listed technical submissions include scaled sketch/lot and vicinity plans, relocation survey plans/reports signed/sealed by a licensed Geodetic Engineer (4 copies); technical specifications signed/sealed by a licensed Architect (2 copies); bill of materials/cost estimates signed/sealed by a licensed Architect (4 copies); seismic analysis; clear detailed location photographs with landmarks or Google Maps image.',[(4,'16. Sketch','Conditional Requirements')]),
('Additional clearances are conditional: DPWH for structures along a National Highway; CAAP for tall structures; DENR ECC for environmentally critical projects; drainage clearance where stated; traffic impact assessment with site development/parking plans for major development; and RROW clearance for structures along City/Barangay/Subdivision roads. These rows list 1 original and 1 photocopy and preserve their stated conditions.',[(4,'c. Structures','Civil Aviation Authority of the Philippines'),(5,'e. Environmentally','If the applicant is NOT')])],['Correct forms-versus-plans quantities and include omitted Electronics.','Do not silently fix Mechanical row professional/quantity conflicts.','Restore other plan/clearance evidence; do not call conditional clearances universal.'],{'type':'blocking_source_conflict','question':'Confirm Mechanical-plan set count and licensed signing professional: the printed row conflicts internally and names Electronics Engineer.','source':'OCBO PDF3/printed491 row8','blocking':'Mechanical subclaim cannot be certified until clarified.'},'source_conflict_requires_clarification')
review('SCENARIO-OCBO-002',[
('Conditional requirements state: construction/minor repair of buildings 3 storeys and above requires Construction Safety & Health Program, 1 original and 1 photocopy, with DOLE listed under Where to Secure. Boring and Plate Load Test Result/Report is listed if the structure is at least three storeys, 2 copies, with a licensed Civil/Geotechnical Engineer listed. For an additional storey, submit an affidavit that the foundation can carry the proposed additional floors, 2 originals.',[(4,'Conditional Requirements','c. Structures')])],['Preserve source conditions and quantities, including two affidavit originals.','The row does not expressly state signed/sealed report or DOLE approved; avoid adding qualifiers not written here.'])
review('SCENARIO-OCBO-003',[
('Occupancy checklist: application letter (1 original); authorization letter if applicant is not owner (1 original); owner ID with 3 specimen signatures (1 photocopy); Certificate of Occupancy (1 original); Certificate of Completion (1 original); BFP Fire Safety Inspection Certificate (1 original); four-elevation project pictures (front/back/left/right); approved Building Construction, Architectural, Civil/Structural, Sanitary/Plumbing, Electrical and Mechanical installation permits (1 photocopy); approved building-permit plan (1 original).',[(13,'1. Application','10. If the project')]),
('If a different professional undertook/was assigned the project, the checklist requires a signed, notarized waiver from the previous professional in charge (1 original). It also lists Structure Images with CAAP clearance and structural survey for actual building height, signed/sealed by a licensed Geodetic Engineer. The authorization-letter source cell says CPDO and the picture source cell says Hired Geodetic Engineer; those unusual source associations are preserved.',[(13,'10. If the project','CLIENT STEPS'),(13,'2. Authorization','4. Certificate'),(13,'7. Pictures','8. Approved')])],['Restore omitted checklist rows.','Remove as-built-if-altered clause not supported by this OCBO checklist; do not import BFP requirements into OCBO evidence.','Preserve unusual Where to Secure associations rather than invent replacements.'])
review('SCENARIO-OCBO-004',[
('While the Building Permit is being processed, the Building Official may issue GP&EP for foundation subject to line-and-grade verification, inspection and review. It is valid only for 30 days or superseded upon Building Permit issuance. Fees: inspection/verification PHP200; excavation PHP3 per cubic meter; GP&EP issuance PHP50; foundation excavation with basement PHP4 per cubic meter; excavation other than foundation/basement PHP3 per cubic meter; permitted footing/foundation encroachment into public areas PHP250 per square meter or fraction thereof.',[(42,'While the application','250.00')])],['Core rates/validity supported.','Restore verification conditions, non-foundation excavation row and encroachment fraction wording.'])
review('SCENARIO-OCBO-005',[
('Fencing checklist: permit form with 3 sets of Civil/Architectural plans signed/sealed by licensed Civil Engineer/Architect (A3 structural-plan option stated); certified land title and property tax declaration (1 original and 1 photocopy each); the next row repeats Certified True Copy of Tax Declaration of the Property with CTO as source; Barangay Clearance (1 original and 1 photocopy); scaled sketch/lot/vicinity plan signed/sealed by licensed Geodetic Engineer (3 sets); bill of materials/cost estimates signed/sealed by licensed Civil Engineer (3 sets); signing professionals PRC ID/current PTR (1 photocopy); owner/applicant ID with 3 specimen signatures (1 photocopy); conditional DPWH clearance along a National Highway.',[(29,'CHECKLIST','Department of Public Works and Highways')]),
('Fee schedule: masonry/metal/concrete up to 1.80m PHP3 per linear meter; over 1.80m PHP4 per linear meter. Both source rows print "of fraction thereof". Indigenous materials, barbed, chicken or hog wire: PHP2.40 per linear meter. The service introduction says a fence not exceeding 1.80m, while the fee table includes over-1.80m; preserve both rather than infer an eligibility rule.',[(35,'Made of masonry','2.40 per linear meter'),(29,'A Fencing Permit','high')])],['Restore omitted documents/quantities/professional conditions.','Do not silently substitute tax receipt for duplicated tax declaration.','Flag height-scope discrepancy.'],{'type':'official_source_clarification','question':'Confirm duplicated Tax Declaration/CTO row and permit scope for fences above 1.80m; the introduction and fee table differ.','source':'OCBO PDF29/printed517 and PDF35/printed523','blocking':'Affected checklist/scope interpretations only.'},'needs_correction_with_source_ambiguity')
review('SCENARIO-OCBO-006',[
('For a Certified True Copy, submit request letter; photocopy of Building Permit and other related documents; owner valid-ID photocopy with 3 signatures; if not owner, processor valid-ID photocopy with 3 signatures and original SPA; if lost, original Affidavit of Loss. The checklist does not offer reference details as a substitute for the photocopy.',[(103,'CHECKLIST','CLIENT STEPS')]),
('Pay PHP50 per document (1 copy) at the City Treasurer\u2019s Office. The printed TOTAL is 2 Days, 1 Hour, and 19 Minutes. Preserve this as the source-listed total, not an independently verified sum: listed steps include two separate 3-hour entries plus 2 days and other minutes.',[(104,'2. Claim','Office'),(104,'TOTAL','1 copy'),(103,'1. Submit','3 Hours'),(104,'1.3 Forward','2 Days')])],['Restore processor three-signature requirement and original SPA.','Remove unsupported reference-details substitute and notarized adjective absent from this checklist.','Flag inconsistent processing total rather than silently recalculate.'],{'type':'conditional_source_clarification','question':'If using exact turnaround as a validated performance target, confirm printed TOTAL against listed step durations.','source':'OCBO PDF103-104/printed591-592','blocking':'No block to clearly labeling it as printed TOTAL.'})
